/** @mainpage %Qore dataframe Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section dataframeintro dataframe Module Introduction

    The \c dataframe module provides a columnar DataFrame data structure for the
    <a href="../../lang/html/index.html">Qore programming language</a>, enabling
    typed, SQL-like data manipulation for enterprise data science workloads.

    Features:
    - Typed columns: \c float64 (Eigen3-backed), \c int64, \c string, \c bool, \c date
    - Null/missing value support with per-column null masks
    - SQL-like operations: select, filter, sort, groupby, join, valueCounts, nunique,
      pivot, melt, missing-data cleanup, and window functions
    - Dense column interop with \c buffer<T> and @ref Qore::SQL::ColumnarResult "ColumnarResult"
      for SQL and pipeline workloads
    - Native plugin-operator support: \c frame["column"] for columns,
      \c frame[row] for row hashes, \c frame[start..stop] for row slices, and
      \c frame[mask] for predicate masks
    - I/O: CSV (streaming reader), Parquet via Apache Arrow, database (Qore DBI)
    - ML integration: toMatrix/toVector/fromMatrix for zero-overhead ML feeding
    - Thread-safe with cooperative cancellation support

    String values and column names are kept whole, including any NUL characters: a NUL character is data, and it
    is kept through every operation, CSV, Parquet and Arrow IPC, and conversion back to %Qore values.  A column name
    with a NUL character cannot be a hash key, so the methods returning column names as hash keys (such as
    @ref Qore::DataFrame::DataFrame::toRecords() "DataFrame::toRecords()") raise \c HASH-KEY-ERROR for one, and a
    file path with a NUL character, which would name another file, raises \c DATAFRAME-IO-ERROR.

    The files read and written by @ref Qore::DataFrame::DataFrame::readCSV() "DataFrame::readCSV()",
    @ref Qore::DataFrame::DataFrame::writeCSV() "DataFrame::writeCSV()",
    @ref Qore::DataFrame::DataFrame::readParquet() "DataFrame::readParquet()" and
    @ref Qore::DataFrame::DataFrame::writeParquet() "DataFrame::writeParquet()" are subject to the filesystem sandbox
    of the calling program: a file the sandbox does not allow to be read or written raises
    \c FILESYSTEM-ACCESS-DENIED, and a refused write creates or changes no file.

    A column of type \c auto can hold any %Qore value, objects included, and a reference cycle through such a value
    (an object in a DataFrame cell that refers to the DataFrame, for example) is collected by the deterministic
    garbage collector as one through the members of an object is.  A DataFrame returned by an operation shares the
    columns of the DataFrame it was made from, except a column holding objects, closures or references (also in
    lists or hashes), which it gets its own copy of.  A @ref Qore::DataFrame::ColumnRef "ColumnRef" holds its
    DataFrame, and a @ref Qore::DataFrame::GroupedDataFrame "GroupedDataFrame" the columns of its DataFrame, where
    the garbage collector follows them as well.

    To use this module, use \c "%requires dataframe" in your code.

